WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
Take a long glass tube.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.190
Push cotton wool soaked
in ammonia into one end,

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.370
and cotton wool soaked in
hydrochloric acid into the other.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.810
Seal both ends, and wait.

5
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.650
Nobody stirs or pumps anything.

6
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.270
Yet a few minutes later, a white
ring appears inside the tube,

7
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.370
where the two gases have met.

8
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.390
But it doesn't form in the middle.

9
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.710
It forms closer to one end.

10
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.130
Why off-centre?

11
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.510
In this mission, you'll see how
temperature and pressure change

12
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.300
a gas.

13
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.170
You'll find out how random
particle motion spreads gases out,

14
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.050
and how that explains diffusion.

15
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.470
Your mission: explain why the
white ring forms off-centre.
